<!-- ABSTRACT -->
<section class="page page-break">
    <h2>Abstract</h2>

    <p>
        Students often need to manage multiple academic responsibilities,
        including classes, assignments, quizzes, examinations, projects,
        and personal commitments. Without an organized planning system,
        they may experience difficulty prioritizing tasks, managing time,
        and monitoring academic progress.
    </p>

    <p>
        The proposed AI Study Planner is a student-centered application
        designed to organize academic tasks and support daily study
        planning. It will provide features for managing subjects,
        deadlines, task priorities, study schedules, reminders, and
        progress tracking. A recommendation component is planned to help
        students prioritize tasks using factors such as due dates,
        estimated duration, and importance.
    </p>

    <p>
        The proposed technology stack includes Flutter and Dart for the
        mobile interface, Firebase Authentication for user
        authentication, Cloud Firestore for data storage, and Node.js
        with Express.js for backend API services. The system will be
        developed and tested incrementally. The project aims to provide
        a practical and accessible academic planning solution for
        students.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Introduction and Background</h2>

    <p>
        Effective time management is an important part of academic
        success. Students frequently handle several subjects and
        deadlines simultaneously. Traditional methods, such as paper
        diaries and separate reminder applications, may not provide a
        unified view of academic activities.
    </p>

    <p>
        The AI Study Planner proposes a centralized platform where
        students can record tasks, organize their schedules, and review
        their progress. The system is intended to make academic planning
        more structured and easier to manage.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Problem Statement</h2>

    <p>
        Students may find it difficult to prioritize assignments,
        remember deadlines, estimate study time, and maintain a
        consistent routine. Information distributed across notebooks,
        calendars, and messaging applications can make planning
        inefficient.
    </p>

    <p>
        Therefore, a unified academic planning application is proposed
        to help students organize their responsibilities and make
        informed decisions about how to use their available study time.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Aim and Objectives</h2>

    <h3>3.1 Aim</h3>
    <p>
        To design and develop an academic planning application that
        helps students organize study tasks, manage deadlines, and
        monitor their study progress.
    </p>

    <h3>3.2 Objectives</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Provide secure user registration and login.</li>
        <li>Allow students to create and manage subjects and tasks.</li>
        <li>Record deadlines, task priorities, and estimated durations.</li>
        <li>Generate an organized daily study plan.</li>
        <li>Provide reminders for upcoming deadlines.</li>
        <li>Track completed and pending tasks.</li>
        <li>Explore task-prioritization recommendations.</li>
        <li>Develop a user-friendly and maintainable application.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

