    <h2>9. System Development Methodology</h2>

    <p>
        An iterative development approach is proposed. The project will
        be divided into manageable stages. Each stage will produce a
        reviewable result and allow feedback before additional features
        are introduced.
    </p>

    <ol>
        <li>Requirement collection and analysis.</li>
        <li>Interface and system design.</li>
        <li>Database and backend planning.</li>
        <li>Implementation of core features.</li>
        <li>Integration and testing.</li>
        <li>Evaluation, documentation, and final presentation.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>10. Proposed System Architecture</h2>

    <table>
        <tr>
            <th>Layer</th>
            <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Presentation Layer</td>
            <td>Flutter and Dart provide the mobile user interface.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Authentication Layer</td>
            <td>Firebase Authentication manages user identity and sign-in.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Backend Layer</td>
            <td>Node.js and Express.js provide planned API endpoints and application logic.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Data Layer</td>
            <td>Cloud Firestore stores user, subject, task, and progress information.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Planning Component</td>
            <td>A planned prioritization module ranks tasks using urgency, importance, and estimated duration.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <p>
        The exact communication flow between the backend and database
